<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Stockholm (1813)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1813</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-sixth-coalition">War of the Sixth Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm">Stockholm</a> of 3 March 1813 was an alliance between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. Sweden, led by Crown Prince Charles John, agreed to send an army to fight in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, and Britain promised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subsidy">subsidies</a>, supported Swedish ambitions to acquire <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and ceded the French island of Guadeloupe to Sweden. Sweden then joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-sixth-coalition">War of the Sixth Coalition</a>.</p></div>
